  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A wave is travelling from medium 1 to medium 2.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Medium 1 has a refractive index n<sub>1</sub> and medium 2 has a refractive index n<sub>2</sub>. The wavelength of the wave in medium 1 is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span><sub>1</sub> and in medium 2 is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span><sub>2</sub>. What is correct for the comparison of the refractive indices and wavelengths?</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
